message.reasoning_content:
The compilation error shows that the interface variables (inputs and outputs) are not being recognized. Looking at the error messages:

- "Unknown type: 'Weld_E_Stop_NC'"
- "Identifier 'Weld_E_Stop_NC' not defined"
- "Identifier 'Operator_Alert' not defined"
- "'Operator_Alert' is no valid assignment target"

This suggests that the VAR_INPUT and VAR_OUTPUT sections are missing or improperly declared. The function block needs to declare the input and output variables in the proper VAR_INPUT/VAR_OUTPUT sections.

Let me look at the candidate code - it seems like the VAR section only has the timer variables, but it's missing the input/output declarations.

The current code has:
```st
VAR
    // Power-up initialization timer: 5-second inhibit period
    PowerUpTimer: TON;
    // Gap signal debounce timer during normal monitoring
    DebounceTimer: TON;
END_VAR
```

It should have:
```st
VAR_INPUT
    Gap_Exceeded: BOOL;
    Weld_E_Stop_NC: BOOL;
    DebounceTime: TIME;
END_VAR

VAR_OUTPUT
    Operator_Alert: BOOL;
    Weld_Soft_Start_Active: BOOL;
END_VAR

VAR
    // Power-up initialization timer: 5-second inhibit period
    PowerUpTimer: TON;
    // Gap signal debounce timer during normal monitoring
    DebounceTimer: TON;
END_VAR
```

The fix is to add the proper VAR_INPUT and VAR_OUTPUT sections with the interface declarations.

